# Files in the repo root that should NOT be served as part of the site.
#
# wrangler.jsonc sets `assets.directory` to ".", so by default every file in
# the repository is published, including internal planning documents. Nothing
# here is secret, but docs/PRD.md is an internal roadmap and there is no reason
# for it to have a public URL.
#
# Syntax is gitignore-style. Anything NOT listed here is still served, so the
# pages, css/, js/ and data/ are untouched.

# Internal documentation and planning
docs/
README.md

# Build, test and data-refresh tooling (Python; never executed by the site)
scripts/

# Input to scripts/update_metrics.py, not a site asset. No .html or .js
# references it, and deploy.yml already excluded it from the GitHub Pages build
# without this file being kept in step.
#
# It has to be here, not merely ought to be: on 2026-09-01 a routine metrics
# refresh (90f6dcf) grew it from 22.8 MB past Cloudflare's 25 MiB per-file
# upload limit, which fails the WHOLE deployment. The site stopped updating and
# the only symptom was a red build. scripts/check_asset_sizes.py now catches
# this class of failure before a push.
data/symphony_scores.json

# The full database and its file:// twin, 19 MiB each and growing every week.
# Closes PRD open question 2.
#
# NOT a runtime asset, despite the name pairing with database.html. That page
# loads data/database_summary.js, a 3.86 MiB columnar export carrying the same
# 6,816 rows and 29 of the 37 fields (the V1.16 page-weight work). Verified
# three ways before excluding these: no page lists data/database.js in a
# <script src>, nothing anywhere reads the window.DATABASE_DATA global it
# defines, and database.html's only data path is database_summary, with a
# detail modal that renders from a row already in memory rather than fetching.
#
# The eight fields held ONLY here (active_asset_nodes, annualized_turnover,
# cumulative_return, herfindahl_index, max, mean, min, total_costs) are joined
# in at BUILD time by scripts/build_strategy_extras.py, which writes the 0.06
# MiB data/strategy_extras.json that strategies.html actually loads. That
# script's own docstring gives the reason: a browser-side join against 6,669
# entries was rejected on page weight.
#
# So this is a build input, not a site asset, and serving it was the accident:
# a stranger could pull 38 MiB the site itself never requests. Excluding it
# also takes the two largest served files off the path to the 25 MiB per-file
# limit that broke the deployment on 2026-09-01.
#
# IMPORTANT: this file is NOT .gitignore. Both stay committed and on disk, and
# the 17 scripts that read them, including two of the five deploy gates, are
# unaffected.
data/database.json
data/database.js

# Local UI mockups: gitignored as well, listed here as a second line of defence
_wf-mockup.html
_harness_*.html
_harness_*_driver.js

# Repo and tooling config.
#
# `.git/` is listed defensively. wrangler may well exclude it already, but a
# build log reported reading 140 files from the assets directory where a clean
# clone holds 91 tracked ones, and the likeliest remainder is the repository
# itself. If it were served, /.git/ would expose the full history and every
# stray file ever committed. One line closes the question either way.
.git/
wrangler.jsonc
.gitignore
.assetsignore
.github/

# Brand identity work: concepts, the logo system, the brand kit, the guidelines
# and every render check. Committed so it is versioned and backed up, excluded
# here so the served site is unchanged by it.
#
# This entry is what keeps that promise. wrangler.jsonc sets assets.directory
# to ".", so anything NOT listed in this file is published: without these two
# lines, committing the brand work would add 104 public URLs and 4.6 MB to the
# site, including a 539 KB PDF and 2.5 MB of contact sheets that exist only as
# evidence for a design decision.
#
# NOT .gitignore. Everything here stays committed and on disk. The one brand
# file that is gitignored is brand/brand-design.html, and that is a separate
# decision recorded in docs/PRD.md.
brand/
